# Copy to .env and fill in what you need. Nothing here is required: `make`
# runs offline, with no key and no database, and every optional piece that is
# missing turns into a named skip rather than a failure.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must stay that way. Nothing in this file is a real
# value; every line is a placeholder.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- the model
# Only read by `make live` and `python -m tools.live`. Without one of these the
# system drafts with its rule-following reference reasoner, which needs no key
# and no network, and the rest of the pipeline is identical.

# Default provider. Has free models; `python -m tools.live --list-free` lists
# the ones answering right now.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-your-key-here

# Only for --provider anthropic. ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN is the alternative when
# a gateway issues short-lived tokens instead of keys; set one or the other.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=your-gateway-token

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- the store
# With no database reachable the store falls back to append-only JSONL files
# and says which backend answered, on the page and at /health.

# Postgres, if you want one. docker compose up sets this up for you.
# CLINICIAN_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://clinician:clinician@localhost:5544/clinician

# Where the file backend writes. Default: .store
# CLINICIAN_STORE=.store

# Stay on files even with a database running. Useful for a laptop and set by
# the test suite, so no test can write into a real deployment's tables.
# CLINICIAN_STORE_BACKEND=files

# Re-run work even when a stored result would match. The second `make` is fast
# because it replays; this is how you make it do the work again.
# CLINICIAN_FRESH=1

# ------------------------------------------------------------ the deployment

# Interface and port for the surface. A platform usually sets PORT itself.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8000

# Marks a public deployment. The page says so, and the reset button is refused
# unless CLINICIAN_ALLOW_RESET says otherwise.
# CLINICIAN_HOSTED=1

# Permit or refuse the button that destroys the store. Defaults to on locally
# and off on a hosted deployment.
# CLINICIAN_ALLOW_RESET=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the logs
# Structured JSON on stderr. There is no hosted log drain and no SaaS error
# tracker by design: a stack trace here can carry the record that produced it,
# and health data must be processed in-country.

# debug | info | warning | error. Default: info
# CLINICIAN_LOG_LEVEL=info

# plain makes them readable for a person rather than for a machine.
# CLINICIAN_LOG_FORMAT=plain

# ------------------------------------------------------------- the validator
# The official HL7 FHIR validator jar, 190 MB, fetched once by
# `python -m tools.validate_fhir --download`. Absent, the run says so and
# skips it rather than failing.
# FHIR_VALIDATOR_JAR=.tools/validator_cli.jar
